# UI Feedback States

Purpose: consistent async and error presentation in the UI.

## Mandatory rules

- Use `AsyncStateScaffold` or equivalent shared wrappers for loading, empty, error, and success.
- Module workspace pages must wrap data content in `AsyncStateScaffold` at the page root — do not hand-roll `CircularProgressIndicator` + `Column` error layouts on new screens.
- Keep feedback high-performance, uniform, simple, and responsive on mobile, tablet, and desktop by reusing `frontend/lib/shared/` components.
- Keep feedback design simple and intuitive; avoid complex or decorative error layouts that confuse clinical workflows.
- Use design tokens exclusively for colors, spacing, and typography in feedback states — no hard-coded values ([`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc)).
- Reflect successful shared-data changes immediately from Riverpod; backend realtime events reconcile subsequent changes (HTTP persists, WebSocket reconciles).
- Do not expose raw technical errors or exception text to users.
- Keep user-facing error messages localized.
- Provide retry actions for recoverable failures.
- Preserve user input on recoverable form failures.
- Log diagnostic details safely without secrets (see [`observability.mdc`](./observability.mdc)).

## Failure categories (UI behavior)

| Category | UI behavior |
|---|---|
| network | retry option |
| validation | field errors or form summary |
| unauthorized | restore session or redirect to login |
| forbidden | forbidden page/state |
| not found | not-found page/state |
| storage | safe fallback or recovery guidance |
| unexpected | generic safe message; diagnostics logged |

Layer-boundary mapping (DTO → typed failures) is owned by [`error_handling.mdc`](./error_handling.mdc).

